17
00:00:32.061 --> 00:00:34.701
They called him Treasure of the

18
00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:35.611
Good Law.

19
00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.020
Six kings, one after another,

20
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.500
had built Nalanda.

21
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.840
A brick wall enclosed it.

22
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.120
One gate opened into the great

23
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.820
college, with eight halls

24
00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:49.340
inside, and monks' courts four

25
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.590
storeys high.

26
00:00:51.122 --> 00:00:52.922
Ten thousand monks lived and

27
00:00:52.922 --> 00:00:54.762
studied there, residents and

28
00:00:54.762 --> 00:00:56.702
visitors. Not only Buddhist

29
00:00:56.702 --> 00:00:59.442
texts. The Vedas, grammar,

30
00:00:59.442 --> 00:01:01.342
medicine, the Sankhya.

31
00:01:01.342 --> 00:01:03.182
About a hundred pulpits were set

32
00:01:03.182 --> 00:01:04.992
